dialect grammar
grammar stdio.dwg.ac1018.snapshot
extension dwg
start document
comment none

# 🎫️26/08/10/ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL-REAL-CODECS-RUNTIME-REUSE-EVOLUTION FG2: real
# `store::ArtifactDsl::print_dsl`/`parse_dsl` shape for `stdio.dwg` (ac1018), read directly from
# `../🦀️component.rs`'s handcrafted `impl store::ArtifactDsl for DwgSnapshot` — replaces the old
# one-line-header ABNF placeholder (`dialect grammar stdio.dwg.snapshot` — 2 tokens on one line,
# rejected by this dialect's parser — plus `%x`/single-quoted-literal/`SP`/`NL` bodies outside this
# dialect's alphabet). `print_dsl` is `wrap_text(envelope, body)` where `body` is
# `encode_dwg(self).iter().map(|b| format!("{b:02x}")).collect()` — `encode_dwg` returns
# `snap.bytes.clone()` verbatim (this artifact never re-derives the byte payload from its typed
# mirror fields; `bytes` IS the ground truth) — so `body` is a CONTINUOUS run of lowercase hex
# digit pairs, no separators, no whitespace, exactly `stdio.binary`'s own DWG-shaped precedent
# (`💾️binary/…/📸️snapshot/📝️text/📖️component.grammar.semio`) — `stdio.dwg` genuinely IS "a binary
# file", same "format is bytes" honest treatment.
#
# `dsl::fixture_sweep::m5_handcrafted_grammar_conformance::dsl_body_from_fixture` (and this
# artifact's own `grammar_conformance_law`, mirroring it) feeds the Recognizer
# `"<envelope-id>\n<body>"` — the mandatory `semio stdio.dwg.dsl v1` preamble line is a
# framework-level envelope concern, already described once at
# 🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🧬️semio/📡️protocol/📡️component.protocol.semio (P2-M3
# deliverable 3) and stripped down to the bare `SemioEnvelope::envelope_id()` (`"stdio.dwg"`)
# before this grammar ever sees it.
document = artifact-mark hex-body
artifact-mark = "stdio.dwg.ac1018"

# P2-P1-fix note (mandatory reading, `p2-p1-fix-report.md`): an open-ended hex run MUST be the
# framework's built-in `hex` MACRO (bare `hex`, no matching production here — `Symbol::Ref` falls
# back production-then-macro automatically), never a hand-rolled `{INT | IDENT}*`-shaped
# production (`Symbol::Star` is a single greedy, non-backtracking pass and silently mis-swallows
# an adjacent keyword-shaped token). `hex-body` is the last token in the document — nothing
# follows it to backtrack off of — and the macro already supports the empty-body case
# (`DwgSnapshot::default()`'s `bytes: vec![]`, though `encode_dwg` itself errors on an empty
# payload — see `../🦀️component.rs`'s `encode_dwg` — so an empty body is grammar-legal but never
# genuinely emitted by `print_dsl`).
hex-body = hex
